                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game could have been fun, when it was at least changed for use on the pc.\n\nIt's a very easy game to understand. capture ports and destroy enemyships. The first time you play it, and every minigame, you get a overwiew with what you should do. So far so good. But then comes the gameplay. It's based for a touch-screen and not adapted for the mouse. So this will happen:\n\nnaval battle's. Before you reach to select your first ships, the enemy has already moved and attacked, and half your ships are killed before you issue your first order. Even if you have 3x more ships. The battle is almost everytime lost.\nPort attacks: You can't press duck and then shoot within a second. You lose lives very fast. \n\nOnly the minibattle to capture the other gold ships is doable.\n\nOfcourse you can choose autoresolve-battle. No minigames. But the game then gets boring. Because the only thing you do is move ships, and buy stuff. The fun part is gone.\n\nSo, don't buy it. And a plea to the developers:\nPlease, make it usable for mouse. F.E. slow the pace of naval battle's, or use a pause function where you can select your ships and issue orders. Slow the pace of capturing ports as well. So you have time to shoot or duck. Or change it to keybord. Number the enemies and by pressing a button let your character shoot or duck. \n\nUntill then, it's a big thumbs down\n",
